  {
   "id": 40,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    60,
    2498
   ],
   "size": [
    900,
    260
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 11,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Cue the Boom: the whole shot as one workflow\n\nLoad your **plate** (an object filmed with the phone held still) and your **performance** (a noise: \"pf.\", \"KA-BOOM\", \"fwoooOOOM\", \"hissss\").\n\n1. **CueSync Analyze Voice** finds your hit, your loudness per frame and when you stop. **CueSync Paint Guide** paints the ainvfx-fluid control video from it: blobs appear on your hit and grow with your voice. Pick the effect and the emission point (x, y) here.\n\n2. **LTX-2.5** with the **ainvfx-fluid** IC-LoRA renders fire, smoke or steam on black following that guide (unchanged from the ainvfx-fluid sample, open weights only).\n\n3. **CueSync Object Matte** (SAM 2.1) finds the object under the emission point; **CueSync Composite** lands the element on your hit, stops it when you stop, keeps the object in front and composites it in linear light.\n\nRepo: github.com/grzenio22/cue-the-boom"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "# Cue the Boom: the whole shot as one workflow\n\nLoad your **plate** (an object filmed with the phone held still) and your **performance** (a noise: \"pf.\", \"KA-BOOM\", \"fwoooOOOM\", \"hissss\").\n\n1. **CueSync Analyze Voice** finds your hit, your loudness per frame and when you stop. **CueSync Paint Guide** paints the ainvfx-fluid control video from it: blobs appear on your hit and grow with your voice. Pick the effect and the emission point (x, y) here.\n\n2. **LTX-2.5** with the **ainvfx-fluid** IC-LoRA renders fire, smoke or steam on black following that guide (unchanged from the ainvfx-fluid sample, open weights only).\n\n3. **CueSync Object Matte** (SAM 2.1) finds the object under the emission point; **CueSync Composite** lands the element on your hit, stops it when you stop, keeps the object in front and composites it in linear light.\n\nRepo: github.com/grzenio22/cue-the-boom"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
